  "solution": {
    "text": "At the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> the energy of the pendulum is entirely potential energy. At point B, the energy of the pendulum is entirely kinetic energy. It means that as the bob pendulum lowers from A to B, the potential energy is converted into kinetic energy. Thus, at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>, KE = PE. But <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the potential energy is dissipated against air resistance.<br /><br /><img src=\"assets\\st0005_c91a98e40b8e.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" /><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KE</mi></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>95</mn><mo>%&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>PE</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>at</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> .... (i)<br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi></math> From equation (i), <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>95</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></math><br /><br /><math><msup><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>95</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>95</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>9.8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1.5</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>19</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>9.8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow><mn>10</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>27.93</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>5.285</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.3</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>"
  }
